# Unit-of-Work Workflow

Implementation follows `plans/00-overview.md` order. Work happens on **`develop`**.

## Cadence

1. Read the unit plan; note Depends on / acceptance criteria
2. If ambiguous, list 2–3 options, pick the recommended one, proceed (unless the user asked to pause)
3. Implement + **unit tests** in the same change
4. Run `npm test` (and `typecheck` / `lint` / `build` when the unit touches packaging)
5. **One commit per unit** — squash any WIP commits into a single unit commit before finishing
6. Update plan status / overview checkmarks when the unit completes
7. **Push to remote only after the unit is complete** (squashed commit on `develop`)

## Pre-Start vs Foundation

- Do not start **C1+** until PRE-C1-A/B/C decisions are recorded
- Spikes stay under `spikes/`; production API stays under `src/`

## Do not

- Commit on `master` for feature units
- Skip Vitest for “small” logic changes
- Expand scope into the next unit inside the same commit
- Push mid-unit WIP; wait until the unit commit is ready
